rization_id a2. Then maybe after commit result we might get receipt? But as next action, commit.\n\nNeed output only JSON object with kind/tool/arguments_json/report_json. arguments_json should be a string containing JSON object? The instruction: \"arguments_json is a JSON-encoded argument object\". Since final answer is JSON object, arguments_json value should be a string, e.g. \"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",...}\". report_json \"{}\". kind \"tool\". tool \"commit\".\n\nNeed ensure valid JSON. No code fences. Let's craft. \n{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4873,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-V-009-c2-a2-1\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\n\nNeed check committed_value type: authorized_value 4873 number. Good.\n\nShould we instead call get_state first? Already did after stale. Last actions: get_state, propose c2, request_authorization a2. So next is commit. Good.\n\nEnsure no extra text. ","signature":"08d55de7-96b8-4599-8672-0369b9b6e398"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4873,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-V-009-c2-a2-1\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":707,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2944,"output_tokens":713,"service_tier":"standard"}}